# Dockerfile-specific build-context allowlist for Dockerfile.remote (H9 review).
#
# Used automatically by BuildKit when building with `-f Dockerfile.remote`
# (falls back to `.dockerignore` on builders without per-Dockerfile support;
# that fallback is UNVERIFIED -- the owner must confirm which ignore file the
# platform builder honors before deployment). No `docker build` has been run.
#
# Default-deny: everything is excluded first, then only the packaging inputs
# and minimal runtime files listed below are re-included. Parent directories
# of re-included files must be re-included explicitly.
#
# Excluded by the default-deny (never sent in build context): .git history,
# secrets (.env files, tokens, keys), virtualenvs (.venv*, venv/), tests/,
# unrelated source (app.py, web.py, meta_agent.py, vision.py,
# external_agent.py, carrier.html), fixtures/, browser assets, screenshots,
# docs/, scripts/, requirements.lock.txt (full local set), and all other files.
**
!Dockerfile.remote
!requirements.remote.lock.txt
!deploy/
!deploy/remote_healthcheck.py
!src/
!src/axle_hackathon/
!src/axle_hackathon/__init__.py
!src/axle_hackathon/remote_app.py
!src/axle_hackathon/axle_api.py
!src/axle_hackathon/schemas.py
!src/axle_hackathon/economics.py
